  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Sanitation Hub</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Deployment of Water Advice and Innovation advisor</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GTO is receiving a grant from Bill &amp; Melinda Gates foundation for the creation of the &apos;Humanitarian Sanitation Hub&apos;. The hub will be a one-stop-shop, for all tools related to emergency sanitation. This hub is an initiative of the Faecal Sludge Management (FSM) Technical Working Group (TWiG) of the global WASH cluster, which is an inter-agency collaborative platform led by the Netherlands Red Cross. In addition to leading the FSM TWiG, NLRC is currently coordinating technical remote support in the field of sanitation to ongoing emergencies. Within this grant with GTO, NLRC is sub-contracted on the specific topic of setting up the personal help-desk for WASH clusters, involved local governments and WASH practicioners facing specific sanitation issues. The help desk will be a formalized and financed version of the remote support that NLRC is already providing through the FSM TWiG. In addition, NLRC will be responsible for validation of the beta-versions of the hub and the provided tools, through our ongoing operational support. We are well placed to do this work as we have a FSM expert in the WAI unit and we already lead the working group on this topic within the Global WASH cluster. The outcome of the project funded by this grant will benefit directly the NS that want to build their capacity on FSM, by having standard and best practices available, but also any other humanitarian organisation. This project contributes to the strategic objective of profiling NLRC in the Water/WASH international space.</narrative>
  </description>
